t and file replay acceptance,\n   128\t  before storage, caching, or exposure. Ordinary reads of accepted snapshots\n   129\t  hash-verify and decode without re-encoding. Validation belongs to the\n   130\t  shared codec/wrapper at those boundaries, not to backend value handlers;\n   131\t  immutable local forwarding does not repeat ingress validation. Missing\n   450\t\n   451\tCarry canonical payload bytes as padded standard-alphabet Base64 strings\n   452\t(no whitespace or URL-safe alphabet) inside the existing Transit\n   453\toperation envelopes. Encode and decode this transport representation at\n   454\tJing's network boundaries; leave general DaoStream Transit unchanged.\n   455\tRemote and DHT APIs above the byte-store wrapper remain value-facing.\n   456\t\n   457\tDecode Base64 strictly, hash-verify received bytes against the claimed\n   458\taddress, and perform the one ingress canonicality check before accepting or\n   459\tcaching them. Preserve explicit presence indicators, idempotent writes,\n   460\tcorrelated remote errors, and DHT refusal/next-candidate behavior. A found\n   461\tnil travels as Base64 of CBOR nil; an absent envelope keeps its explicit\n   462\tfalse indicator and nil placeholder, which is not Base64-decoded.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
